      explain: "**When store billing is required**: digital goods and services consumed in the app (premium features, subscriptions, in-game currency) generally must use Apple's In-App Purchase on iOS and Google Play Billing on Android, subject to regional exceptions (alternative billing or external links where permitted). **Physical goods and real-world services** (food delivery, rides, physical products) use normal payment providers such as Stripe or Razorpay. **Product types**: consumables (coins), non-consumables (unlock forever), auto-renewable subscriptions, and non-renewing subscriptions. **Fees** (headline programmes, before taxes): 30% standard; 15% for Apple Small Business Program members and Google's first $1M per year; subscriptions 15% after the subscriber's first paid year on Apple, and 15% on Google subscriptions. Proceeds are paid out by the stores on their schedules, net of taxes they collect in many countries. Pricing is set in price tiers or per-country prices in the store consoles. Rules evolve (anti-steering, alternative billing, regional programmes), so treat the store guidelines and agreements as configuration that legal and product teams review.",
